var a=Object.defineProperty;var n=(o,e)=>{for(var t in e)a(o,t,{get:e[t],enumerable:!0})};var h=[{text:'Air quality maps beside the temperature map: **CO\u2082**, **Humidity**, **Fine particles (PM2.5)** and **VOC**, from a sensor placed in each room or of its area. The map button steps through those the home has sensors for, a legend gives the bands, and the colours are safe for colour blindness. A room whose air needs something doing says so on its label ("CO\u2082 1,640 ppm").',anchor:"find-your-way-around"},{text:"The temperature map has a legend too, from 16\xB0 to 26\xB0.",anchor:null},{text:"Robot vacuums and mowers move on the plan while they work, with a soft trail where they have been this run: from a map camera with the robot's position (Xiaomi Cloud Map Extractor, MQTT Vacuum Camera), Valetudo's map data, or a mower's GPS tracker. **Its map** (Edit \u2192 Selected) lines the robot's map up with the plan from two spots. Robots without one stay at their dock, their pin showing what they do (red on an error). Smart Setup places mowers on their lawn.",anchor:"by-hand"},{text:"The alarm chip opens an **Alarm** sheet: each panel with what it covers, the doors and windows open there, and arming or disarming that asks first, with the code when the panel wants one. Rooms with a door or window open are tinted orange while it arms (and after Alarmo couldn't arm); when it goes off, the view goes to what set it off (Alarmo's sensor, or the last to go on before) and tints its room red.",anchor:"find-your-way-around"},{text:"Warnings: a banner when it rains, or rain is forecast within the hour, while windows are open (naming them and tinting their rooms; a window can be marked out of the rain), and on a power cut, with the battery left (from a grid status sensor picked under Energy, a UPS on battery, or the grid's power gone while the battery still reports).",anchor:null},{text:"Guide: the Wall Tablet extension's screen control (on when someone is near, brightness) and screensaver, and Fully Kiosk's JavaScript interface.",anchor:null}];export{n as a,h as b};
